# Maintainer: ArchMage contributors
#
# ArchMage desktop layer umbrella (v3, D-0: Omarchy base), x86_64.
#
# The Omarchy 4.5.x base provides the desktop stack itself — Hyprland + uwsm
# + quickshell shell, SDDM, xdg portals, pipewire stack, gum, limine +
# snapper + snap-pac, keyring/settings/themes — via the pinned `omarchy` meta
# package (see test/desktop-x86_64.sh, D-0 plan in
# docs/internal/HANDOFF-OMARCHY-BASE.md). This umbrella therefore carries
# ONLY what the base misses: the CN layer, the CN input method, the
# verification terminal, and the network baseline. Phone-only packages stay
# deliberately absent: cn-apn (modem), archmage-phosh-safety, waydroid stack,
# archmage-btrfs-rollback (phone partition layout). cn-mirror is
# ALARM-specific; the desktop mirror package (archmage-desktop-mirror) is
# D-2' scope.

pkgname=archmage-desktop
pkgver=3
# pkgrel 2: rebuild against the fixed archmage-branding (source= array) so the
# staging repo carries v3 — the PKGDEST cache only ever held v2 (v3 never
# survived a packages run before the branding fix).
pkgrel=2
pkgdesc='ArchMage desktop layer umbrella: CN defaults + fcitx5 + TUI tooling on the Omarchy base (x86_64)'
arch=(x86_64)
url='https://github.com/Arcane-Reflection/ArchMage'
license=(Apache)
depends=(
  # ArchMage brand layer (L1+L2 rebrand engine + archmage session entry)
  'archmage-branding'
  # CN defaults (archmage overlay, any-arch configuration packages)
  'archmage-cn-locale'
  'archmage-cn-fonts-meta'
  'archmage-cn-net'
  # CN input method (fcitx5 wayland IME; --wayland-ime per Omarchy 3.0 fix)
  'fcitx5'
  'fcitx5-chinese-addons'
  'fcitx5-gtk'
  'fcitx5-qt'
  'noto-fonts-cjk'
  # Verification terminal (Omarchy 4.5 ISO defaults to foot; Ghostty stays
  # our CN-input verification target per the D-0 handoff)
  'ghostty'
  # Browser (Omarchy base lists chromium in its ISO set; explicit here so the
  # umbrella is self-contained if installed without the full ISO set)
  'chromium'
  # Network baseline
  'networkmanager'
  'ufw'
  # TUI tooling layer (gum arrives via the omarchy meta package; fzf explicit)
  'fzf'
)

package() {
    install -d "$pkgdir/usr/share/doc/$pkgname"
    cat > "$pkgdir/usr/share/doc/$pkgname/README" <<'DESCEOF'
ArchMage desktop layer umbrella v3 (Omarchy 4.5.x base, D-0).

The base (omarchy meta package) owns: Hyprland + uwsm + quickshell shell,
SDDM, xdg portals, pipewire, gum, limine + limine-snapper-sync + snapper,
keyring/settings/themes-intros. This umbrella adds the ArchMage brand layer
(archmage-branding), the CN default set (locale, CJK fonts, network
defaults), fcitx5 Chinese input, Ghostty, chromium, NetworkManager + ufw.

Management happens through the archmage TUI layer (see ROADMAP.md v0.2).
Phone-only layers (modem APN, phosh shell safety, OSK, waydroid, phone
btrfs rollback layout) are deliberately not pulled in.

Omarchy is MIT (c) Basecamp / omacom-io; attribution in the image docs.
DESCEOF
}
